"edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step5-opus-aa-1017-omp36-aa/omp-36/cells/aa-1/trig-omp-reported/8/workspace", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "aa-2", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/17.3.8 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/5347ff91e8f44f2c69a79d7b152b7301687cd5c8/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Fixed. `test_dates` and the other 2 tests in `tests/` pass.\n\n**Cause:** `parse_date` used `strptime` with the format `\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"`. That format has no slot for a UTC marker, so the trailing `Z` in `2026-10-12T08:30:00Z` was left over and raised the error.\n\n**Fix** in `dates/parse.py`: `parse_date` now calls `datetime.fromisoformat(s)`. On Python 3.11 and later (this machine has 3.13.5), that function accepts a trailing `Z`, offsets like `+02:00`, and timestamps with no zone.\n\n**One behaviour change:** timestamps ending in `Z` now come back with the UTC timezone attached (`tzinfo=timezone.utc`). Timestamps without a zone still come back with none. Comparing or subtracting one kind against the other raises `TypeError`, so watch for that if any other code mixes them. `day_key` is unaffected, since it only formats the date.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 25494, "requests_cache_write": 103879, "requests_cost_usd": 0.5456818000000001, "requests